HOW TO READ THIS
==========================================================================
  Steering toward EXPERT (positive alpha) predicts: jargon up,
  defining down, scaffolding down, words down.
  Toward NOVICE (negative alpha): the reverse.

  If jargon slope is significant and outputs are not degraded,
  the direction is causally used -- that is the finding this
  whole project was missing.

  If nothing moves, say so: the direction is decodable but not
  demonstrably used. That is TalkTuner's reading/control gap and
  it is worth reporting.

  READ THE ACTUAL TEXT before believing any of these numbers.
  It is all in data/qwen35-4b/steer_results.json.

